# What each segment of enus is made of, as targets.
#
# A `base' line is what a phoneme's parameter does at a stress, whatever
# is either side of it. Any other line names the phoneme to the left and
# the one to the right, `.' for a word edge, and says what that context
# does instead.
#
# The numbers are the targets the parameter reaches, in order. What it
# starts from is whatever the segment before left behind and is not here;
# how long each stretch takes is the duration model's and is not either.
#
# Harvested by tools/module/segments.py. See docs/authoring.md.
